WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 008, en. Timings are estimates from the script until the clip is rendered.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.231
<v the Bute estate agent>Bore da, Miss Nia. Mind the ink, it's still drying. This is Mr David Stewart's survey of the Bute estates, eighteen twenty-four. Plan nineteen.

2
00:00:09.581 --> 00:00:23.042
<v Nia>Cedfin or Ty Mawr Farm. Two names for one farm, side by side. Today the Glamorgan Archives catalogue files it as Cedfin alias Ty Mawr farm, in Llandough, reference D B E one to two.

3
00:00:23.392 --> 00:00:31.085
<v the Bute estate agent>One hundred and thirty-nine acres, three roods, eight perches. Of that, twenty acres, two roods and thirty-five perches is woodland.

4
00:00:31.435 --> 00:00:39.512
<v Nia>And the occupier? I read that hand as John Gedrick, but I'd want a second pair of eyes on those letters.

5
00:00:39.862 --> 00:00:47.554
<v the Bute estate agent>Gedrick, near enough. And mark this corner: ten acres, three roods, thirty-nine perches of late Thos. Williams land, added in.

6
00:00:47.904 --> 00:00:58.673
<v Nia>A Williams on this ground in eighteen twenty-four. The plan shows his land joined to Ty Mawr. It doesn't show who he was, or how it came across.

7
00:00:59.023 --> 00:01:14.023
<v Nia>The family wiki holds an uploaded picture titled eighteen twenty-four map of Ty Mawr. Nobody has pinned down who drew it, its scale, its sheet, where the original lives, or whether eighteen twenty-four is even the map's own date.

8
00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:19.373
<v the Bute estate agent>Then lay it beside plan nineteen, madam, and let the lines settle it.

9
00:01:19.723 --> 00:01:25.108
<v Nia>Exactly. Until they're matched, it's a picture, not proof of any boundary registered later.

10
00:01:25.458 --> 00:01:34.304
<v Nia>Then this one, saved in the media library as eighteen forty-one map. No title we can trust, no survey date, no archive number.

11
00:01:34.654 --> 00:01:40.423
<v the Bute estate agent>Seventeen years after Mr Stewart? Then the tithe men will have been busy in Llandough.

12
00:01:40.773 --> 00:01:49.619
<v Nia>They were. The eighteen forty-one tithe apportionment for Llandough, Cogan and Leckwith survives as the parish copy, Glamorgan Archives P thirty-five stroke ten.

13
00:01:49.969 --> 00:01:56.892
<v Nia>But nothing yet ties this image to that apportionment, and neither picture proves ownership, possession or any conveyance.

14
00:01:57.242 --> 00:01:59.935
<v the Bute estate agent>Then you'll be wanting the apportionment itself.

15
00:02:00.285 --> 00:02:07.208
<v Nia>First thing tomorrow. Let's follow those Williamses forward and see when Great House farm turns up in print.
